{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1182398-trinity-vs-scion-compare-and-contrast","id":1182398,"title":"Trinity vs. Scion: compare and contrast","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-02-04T15:03:41-08:00","id":1182398,"title":"Trinity vs. Scion: compare and contrast","content":"I'm posting this in the Trinity forum because at the time of this post, the Trinity Kickstarter is still in its early stages, and only part of the manuscript has been revealed to backers. Nonetheless, there are some very interesting reveals thus far in terms of how TC compares to Scion \u2014 issues that will need to be addressed by any gaming group that seeks to combine the two. Off the top of my head:<br /> <br /> 1. TC baselines are fundamentally more competent than Scion mortals: their Paths give them Edges, and their Skills give them Skill Tricks. By contrast, Scion mortals get specialties for their Skills but no Skill Tricks, and the ones with Supernatural Origins get a single Knack. Note that the sample Skill Tricks and Edges cover a lot of ground that used to be covered by Heroic Knacks in Adventure!. <br /> <br /> 2. OTOH, Scion mortals tend to have slightly higher attributes (they get two dots instead of one in each Attribute of their favored Approach), and <i>everyone</i> has access to Twists of Fate, the Scion counterpart to Dramatic Editing: all they need to do is to spend successes from a relevant roll and the setting adjusts more to their liking. Conversely, it looks like Dramatic Editing is going to be restricted to Talents: psiads, psions, novas, and aberrants (paraphrasing) \u201creject flux and seek to strengthen their native realities,\u201d and baselines presumably don't have the ability in the first place. <br /> <br /> When combining the two, my inclination would be to use TC's baselines as, well, the baseline, with Twists of Fate added in and Talents using their Inspiration to take things a step further. That said, I may change my mind once I see TC's Dramatic Editing rules (which have not yet been released).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-06T14:35:15-08:00","id":1183043,"title":"","content":"I keep hearing about red and black pools in Scion. Is one of those pools analogous to Momentum in Trinity?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-06T17:30:46-08:00","id":1183103,"title":"","content":"The final text might change the terminology a bit - Neall has said that Scion 2e's text still has a bunch of legacy terms in it - since red and black pools were terms to differentiate between SG and player pools.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-06T17:49:53-08:00","id":1183110,"title":"","content":"The black pool is Momentum, and at least according to the Polyhedron interview last night with Ian, Danielle, and Eddy, the red pool is gone.<br /> <br /> I can't speak for Trinity, but I feel like that metamorphosized into Tension for Scion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1897-ffanxii4ever","name":"ffanxii4ever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-06T20:08:05-08:00","id":1183137,"title":"","content":"Correct: The Black Pool was initially intended to be the Momentum Pool available to players, while the Red Pool was the Momentum available to the Storyguide. We trimmed out the latter. Just replace any references to the Black Pool with &quot;Momentum&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-11T21:46:06-08:00","id":1185014,"title":"","content":"Edit: The first column is the combined skill list. The second is the Scion preview list. Then the Trinity list is last. Special notes; Aim is not an exact parallel to Firearms, as bows and thrown weapons are covered by Athletics in Scion at the moment.<br /> <br /> Skills__________Scion______Trinity <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"border-spacing: 0px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Academics</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Academics</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"b